## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current product/platform authority. Existing domain-specific safety rules in this file remain valid.

New roadmap issues/epics do not enable capabilities. Preserve fail-closed server/client gates until an explicit rollout issue authorizes production enablement. Do not add mock Channels/Groups/Desktop/Mobile merely to satisfy navigation/design screenshots.



# Real product data

Production UI must read real API/session/domain data. Never copy demo content from design PNGs.

No fake production routes, arrays, users, projects, conversations, counts, prices, usage or notification states.

Implemented-but-disabled capabilities (for example Direct Chats, Projects, @Vimla Operator, Memory/orchestration) must stay behind their genuine fail-closed server/client gates. Not-yet-implemented roadmap capabilities (for example Groups, Channels, Desktop/Mobile apps or later creator/platform features) may appear only as dev/test presentation references with no fake production behavior.

Empty/loading/error/disabled states are preferred to pretending a missing backend exists.
